{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1536307-how-do-you-handle-disciplines-in-games-that-begin-with-the-pcs-first-night","id":1536307,"title":"How do you handle Disciplines in games that begin with the PCs first night?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-05-26T10:30:56-07:00","id":1536307,"title":"How do you handle Disciplines in games that begin with the PCs first night?","content":"I've occasionally run games where the story begins with their first night awakening, and the characters don't even immediately know that they are vampires. In such games, I'll have the first three dots manifest spontaneously when attempting something. Like someone will try to escape a locked door, and they will spontaneously manifest Potence or grow claws.<br /> <br /> Do you handle the first night similarly, or do you have them spend long periods of time post-embrace learning those first three dots?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-26T11:30:46-07:00","id":1536311,"title":"","content":"It depends on the disciplines involved, the clans, and the players.<br /> <br /> There have been many times where I had the Player roll randomly in the middle of a situation to see if a discipline activates. So, a freshly turned Toreador might accidentally activate their Auspex sense enhancement while driving, which partially blinds them due to oncoming headlights. Alternatively, if they are trying to slip through a crowd of mortals at a bar unnoticed, their Presence might activate. Generally, I don't have things activate if it burns blood/WP, unless it would work out in their favor in the given situation, such as activating Celerity to dodge far enough to avoid getting hit by a truck or semi.<br /> <br /> The random activations reinforce the notion of learning how to walk which can be helpful for immersion, but after the first couple of nights they have the hang of it. The only exception being the various blood magics, those tend to take time to figure out. So, a new Tremere would get their Auspex and Dominate down in a night or two, but the Thaumaturgy &amp; Rituals that will take longer, often with some storyline involved.<br /> <br /> The weird one out is Fortitude when it comes to understanding how it works for a freshly embraced vampire. Due to how damage isn't a fixed value, and your soak isn't a fixed value, you always have a chance of damage. So, a newly embraced vampire with one dot of Fortitude might run a knife blade over their palm and do nothing one time, but then try it a second time and slash their hand. It's kind of like superman being bullet proof 75% of the time, it raises more questions than just being immune to a damage type/situation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-27T12:28:43-07:00","id":1536378,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1536307-how-do-you-handle-disciplines-in-games-that-begin-with-the-pcs-first-night#post1536307\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've occasionally run games where the story begins with their first night awakening, and the characters don't even immediately know that they are vampires. In such games, I'll have the first three dots manifest spontaneously when attempting something. Like someone will try to escape a locked door, and they will spontaneously manifest Potence or grow claws.<br /> <br /> Do you handle the first night similarly, or do you have them spend long periods of time post-embrace learning those first three dots?</div> </div> </div> </div>I usually go with them know the first dot of the physical Disciplines like Celerity, Fortitude and Potence in their first nights then needing help from there mentors to learn things like Animalism, Auspex, Dominate, Obfuscate, Presence or Protean for that matter. But I do consider the backstory of the character and having an affinity for certain Disciplines like my Malkavian knowing a dot of Presence off the bat.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-27T14:12:38-07:00","id":1536382,"title":"","content":"I've never run such games. If I did, I would probably run them differently than how I actually handle that period of a vampire's existence in my chronicles. Which is that vampires only slowly develop their Disciplines over time as they learn to control the inherent powers of the blood. Just like newborn babies don't already know how to walk, be potty-trained, or able to speak languages. It takes effort.. and well, discipline. So for PCs back stories, they learnt their three Discipline dots (or more) that they get at character creation, over the period of back story(typically 5-20 years per the books), though I find many PCs want there to be only 2-3 years between Embrace and when game begins so I accommodate them.<br /> <br /> For NPCs that get embraced during the game, they start with zero Disciplines, and probably get their first dot only after six to twelves months time with more discipline dots only later. They do learn other powers of the blood (like spending boosting stats, healing damage, spending blood to look more alive) much earlier. The only powers they posses right after embrace are passive ones like lethal damage being the same as bashing, having fangs that can do aggravated damage, or creating the blood bond. That means newly made Sabbat shovelheads can't do a whole lot. It also means new vampires often need the help of their sires in order to survive and not break the Masquerade for a long time (the exception of course being the Gangrel who want to observe how their childe can handle things on their own before they introduce themselves).<br /> <br /> If a player wants to run scenes with them just after embrace, I will do that as part of their preludes. Some players like that kind of experience. But they don't know Disciplines right after the embrace. If they want to run scenes like how they learned their first Discipline and so on, again I'll run that as another part of their prelude. I run preludes very collaboratively and without dice rolls so it can accomplish what the player wants for their PC and not derail things prior to them actually playing.<br /> <br /> If I was running a game when game play actually began right after the embrace, I'd do things differently simply because I cannot imagine players having fun without being able to use some Disciplines quite early. But that is recognizing out of character concerns to affect the game play, not part of the actual setting I use in my chronicles.<br /> <br /> However, I've never had players who want to actually roleplay out the entire process of learning about vampire abilities and vampire society. That takes too much time getting the character to the same point as the player. I find running those kind of scenes as a brief prelude usually accomplishes what they want, and cuts down on wasted time. The only time I've ever seen game play begin from the embrace is when brand new players are first introduced to the game so they know nothing about the game setting or mechanics. Their characters learn about the setting as the same time as the players, so there's no sense of waste. In those kind of chronicles, I typically see the PCs get one dot of Discipline per game session.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3046,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","user":"Black Fox","date":".  typos 05-28-2024, 02:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-28T09:35:13-07:00","id":1536436,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1536307-how-do-you-handle-disciplines-in-games-that-begin-with-the-pcs-first-night?p=1536382#post1536382\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've never run such games. If I did, I would probably run them differently than how I actually handle that period of a vampire's existence in my chronicles.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's the point.<br /> <br /> I run NPCs and preludes very similar to your take, and I guess the others do so, too.<br /> <br /> But when actually running a game that starts with the PCs as fledglings, keeping them out of Disciplines for long is simply boring. I usually run things as <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3598_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3598\" data-vbnamecard=\"3598\">CajunKhan</a> does, with occasional changes to experiment with other methods.<br /> <br /> One thing I do, though, is to then reinforce how unusual the PCs are on learning Disciplines so fast. Which is actually quite useful as during the game the system naturally make them learn things at a pace that's incredibly fast lore-wise.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-04T19:45:27-07:00","id":1536826,"title":"","content":"I just go with it based on the given PC's natural affinities and/or pre-existing metaphysical knowledge (if any). This goes pretty well with the loose approach that prior editions of Vampire took in that regard: some (N)PCs were exampled as taking weeks or months+ to develop any dots in their disciplines, while others literally awaken with their affinitive powers already working via instinct/latent in the blood (Ex: the Sleep/Dreamwalker sample Malkavian PC woke up with Auspex:4 after being embraced). So there's no hard or fast rule/guideline I've ever used running Vampire since in came out over 30 years ago. Some characters just do &quot;x&quot; instinctively (media example: Evil Ed having Protean:4 just hours after being embraced, similar to the Malkavian example) while others may just have a dot in each of their clan disciplines after years of being coddled in an extended fledgling-hood under their Sire's (over)care.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have been around here for waaaayyyy too fucking long...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1433-just-john-forever","name":"Just John, Forever...","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-04T20:21:49-07:00","id":1536830,"title":"","content":"Ooo! I once ran a game based of the movie, the Crow, where the player was a vampire, seeking revenge for his murder, but, he didn't know he was a vampire. I had him use a mortal-sheet and the game started with him digging himself out of his grave.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I have all the power in the world to give you, and all you have to do is beg&quot; -Nix<br /> <br /> &quot;There's thing about being a vampire, Frank; it takes a long fucking time to learn how do all the cool shit&quot;. -Abigail","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude0e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","name":"Iguazu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2521_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"738"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}